{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact CDF-1 head 9a1d85ebb7a89100d25d12c56c33a4ee85cf523a on builder/cdf1-scope-bytes-cap-20261113, with carried CF-2 commit 7872d111, all 30 artifacts, for review request df5ef52d under CDF-1 promise 9e716e83 and CF-2 promise d5056d7a. Every scope now counts its retained payload bytes and refuses growth past `scopeBytes`. The count changes only inside the seal transaction, so a refusal rolls back the entry, the rows and the total together.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/scope/src/sqlite.ts`.\n  - `retain` inserts with `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING octet_length(bytes)`, so a row already held adds 0, and each key counts once.\n  - `forget` deletes with `RETURNING` and subtracts the size it removed.\n  - `retainBirth` adds what `retain` adds, and its association row counts nothing.\n  - The constructor fills `retained-bytes` with one `INSERT … SELECT SUM … WHERE NOT EXISTS … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`. An old store therefore gets its total once, in one statement, and a store that has the row keeps it.\n- `packages/scope/src/turn.ts`. `#seal` sums what each `retain` and `retainBirth` adds and returns it with the sealed entry. `#full` first asks the opt-in or `fits` capacity, then `#retainedFull`. That check passes when the entry added nothing. It exempts exactly the inputs that `fits` exempts (`derive/src/reserve.ts:242-243`): a settlement, a timed entry, a diagnosis, an outcome, a control delivery and a result delivery that is not a conflict. Otherwise it refuses when the stored total exceeds `scopeBytes`. The timed path calls `#full` only under `whole-scope`, as before.\n- `core.ts`, `delivery.ts` and `operations.ts` add `name: \"scopeBytes\"` to the existing `scope-full` answer when that bound refused, in every scope. An act gets `refused` and a delivery gets `retry`, as for the other bounds. No reason code, refusal shape or journal form is new.\n- The seal changes in `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs`, for `core.ts:Scope` and `turn.ts`, cover exactly the diffs above. The queue and the timed drain in `turn.ts` don't change.\n- CF-2 item 1, `7872d111`. The header of `base-membership.ts` and the CF-1 note now say that a person revokes a key of their own agent without `membership.own-agent`, and removes that agent only with it. No executable line changes.\n- The contract and `directory.ts` edits change comments only: \"incarnation\" becomes \"genesis\", and one comment now names the create-result kind check.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 4cef11d2 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. Against main, the head changes 28 paths, and the 30 artifacts cover every one: the primary first, 27 path artifacts and the two CF-2 companions. Merge 82bb42da has parents 70f96419 and 4cef11d2, and its tree equals `git merge-tree` of the two.\n- Source correspondence. `git diff --name-only 01bbd802 9a1d85eb` lists four paths, all under `notes/`. Every source, test, configuration and dependency file equals the gate checkpoint.\n- Evidence. The gate manifest's digest is c4b18a91, as the request states.\n  - All five manifests verify against their files: the gate (43 files), the document checks (8), the AC residency file (9), the baseline (13) and the focused runs (24). No file is missing or changed.\n  - The gate's `SHA256SUMS` (b5d0027d) verifies. `gate.exit` is 0, and `head.txt` names 01bbd802 with tree 5f3c41f6.\n  - `gate.stdout` ends \"gate passed\" with no timeout line.\n  - All 58 power samples, from 23:44 to 00:03 EST, read AC Power, and power mode is 0 at START and END. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 23:40 to 00:06.\n- Witnesses. The baseline record shows the four new invariants failing at 5339ccc5 on their own assertions: a value total of 1,416 instead of 4,248, a redaction left at 0 instead of subtracting 10, a fill of 19 instead of 122, and the accepted rule-cap act. These are not setup failures.\n- Cheap checks at the head. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (18 checked, 0 flagged), `git diff --check` is clean, and `check-doc-links` finds 1,245 links with 0 broken. As the request asks, I ran no test, compiler or build beside the builder's slot.\n\nKernel review under `docs/kernel.md` section 7: no objection. The head changes comments only in `packages/contract`, and nothing in `packages/derive` or the kernel part of `packages/bytes`. `Store` lives in `packages/scope`. The new name on `scope-full` is an existing member of `ScopeBoundName`. The head adds no kernel export, no `RefusalReason` member and no journal form, as the request states.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The total is store metadata, written only by `retain` and `forget` in the transaction that writes the rows. No digest, fold or replay reads it, so it can't change a recorded fact. The stop runs after the seal and before the commit, where the opt-in check already runs, and it rolls back as that check does.\n\nSecurity conclusion, as CDF-1 requires: a member can no longer grow a scope's retained payload without limit. Before this head, a scope without the opt-in had no byte cap on retained births, copies, texts, rule inputs, snapshots or values. Now every new retained byte counts, and an ordinary act or request past `scopeBytes` is refused or retried. Three limits stay, each stated and owned:\n\n1. Exempt inputs still add bytes past the bound. A settlement, an outcome or a result can push the total over `scopeBytes`. The pending-work bound limits how many of them can come, but no constant limits their bytes (ruling bb6cf92b, RB-1 0ce66e16).\n2. Only a text redaction frees bytes. A floor frees none, and `retained_value` rows never leave. A scope that reaches the bound stays there for every act that retains something new. FL-1 owns floors in production.\n3. A store already above the bound refuses each new retaining act after the fill. No deployed store exists before the cutover, so no room meets this case.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The expression `definition.declared.capacity || bound === \"scopeBytes\"` now appears in five places. One helper that names the answer for a bound would keep them alike.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing. Plan 036 (approval 7ec380d1) waits for CDF-1 on main.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b96263875cbac0d8522cf45468f78db17688f204","binding":"assigned","head":"9a1d85ebb7a89100d25d12c56c33a4ee85cf523a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e037913dcb86c45ec12becd2799f40e1ad1b28a0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9e716e8356de8f76bcb32579122e16468c51d1d1\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d5056d7aa04796d1448567bb570bed376f7cdbfe\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e037913dcb86c45ec12becd2799f40e1ad1b28a0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}